### Catalogue requests for VS Code REST Client (owner: Jana)
### Click "Send Request" above each request.
### For the staff requests, your .env must contain LOCAL_AUTH=true

# Local (npm start)
@local = http://localhost:3001
# Deployed: paste the CatalogueApiUrl output here after the first deploy
@cloud = https://REPLACE-ME.execute-api.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com

# The fixed IDs from db/seed.sql
@officeA = a1a1a1a1-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@officeB = a1a1a1a1-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@car1 = c0c0c0c0-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@car2 = c0c0c0c0-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@car4 = c0c0c0c0-0000-4000-8000-000000000004

########## Public routes (no login) ##########

### Health check -> 200
GET {{local}}/health

### C7: all offices -> 200, 3 offices
GET {{local}}/offices

### C2: car 1 -> 200 (Hyundai Accent)
GET {{local}}/cars/{{car1}}

### C2: a UUID that does not exist -> 404
GET {{local}}/cars/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### C2: not a UUID -> 400
GET {{local}}/cars/1

### C1: all available cars -> 200, cheapest first
GET {{local}}/cars

### C1: SUVs only -> 200
GET {{local}}/cars?category=suv

### C1: office A, max 1500 EGP/day -> 200
GET {{local}}/cars?office={{officeA}}&maxPrice=1500

### C1: unknown category -> 400
GET {{local}}/cars?category=spaceship

########## Staff routes (pretend login with x-dev-user, local only) ##########

### C6: my office's cars (staff of office A) -> 200
GET {{local}}/offices/{{officeA}}/cars
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

### C6: another office's cars -> 404
GET {{local}}/offices/{{officeB}}/cars
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

### C3: add a car -> 201 (run twice -> 409, same plate)
POST {{local}}/cars
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

{
  "plate": "JNA 777",
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Yaris",
  "category": "economy",
  "dailyPrice": 950
}

### C3: customer tries to add a car -> 403
POST {{local}}/cars
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: customer

{ "plate": "JNA 778", "make": "Toyota", "model": "Yaris", "category": "economy", "dailyPrice": 950 }

### C3: not logged in -> 401
POST {{local}}/cars
Content-Type: application/json

{ "plate": "JNA 779", "make": "Toyota", "model": "Yaris", "category": "economy", "dailyPrice": 950 }

### C4: change car 1's price and put it in maintenance -> 200
PUT {{local}}/cars/{{car1}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

{
  "dailyPrice": 1000,
  "status": "maintenance"
}

### C4: car 4 belongs to office B -> 404 for staff of office A
PUT {{local}}/cars/{{car4}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

{ "dailyPrice": 1 }

### C5: retire car 2 -> 204 (run again -> 404, already retired)
DELETE {{local}}/cars/{{car2}}
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

########## C8 / C9: offices and the map (Nominatim) ##########
### First time only: give the seeded offices their map positions:  npm run geocode-offices

### C8: offices nearest to Nasr City -> 200, nearest first, with distance_km
GET {{local}}/offices/nearest?location=Nasr City, Cairo

### C8: nearest 2 offices to Alexandria -> 200
GET {{local}}/offices/nearest?location=Alexandria&limit=2

### C8: a place that does not exist -> 404
GET {{local}}/offices/nearest?location=Qwertyuiopville

### C8: no location -> 400
GET {{local}}/offices/nearest

### C9: change office A's phone (no map lookup) -> 200
PUT {{local}}/offices/{{officeA}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

{ "phone": "+20 2 1234 5678" }

### C9: change office A's address -> 200, new latitude/longitude from Nominatim
PUT {{local}}/offices/{{officeA}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

{ "address": "Talaat Harb Street, Downtown, Cairo" }

### C9: staff of office A edits office B -> 404
PUT {{local}}/offices/{{officeB}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

{ "name": "Not my office" }

########## C10: price quote (internal, Booking only) ##########
### Locally there is no IAM check, so these work without a login.
### In the cloud, API Gateway returns 403 unless Booking signs the request.

### C10: car 4, 4 days -> 200, total = dailyPrice x 4
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "{{car4}}", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2026-12-05" }

### C10: car 1 in maintenance -> 409 (run the C4 request above first)
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "{{car1}}", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2026-12-05" }

### C10: car 2 retired -> 409 (run the C5 request above first)
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "{{car2}}", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2026-12-05" }

### C10: a UUID that does not exist -> 404
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2026-12-05" }

### C10: carId not a UUID -> 400
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "1", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2026-12-05" }

### C10: missing carId -> 400
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2026-12-05" }

### C10: fake date (30 February) -> 400
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "{{car4}}", "startDate": "2026-02-30", "endDate": "2026-03-02" }

### C10: end before start -> 400
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "{{car4}}", "startDate": "2026-12-05", "endDate": "2026-12-01" }

### C10: more than 30 days -> 400
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "{{car4}}", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2027-01-15" }

### C10: unknown field -> 400
POST {{local}}/internal/quote
Content-Type: application/json

{ "carId": "{{car4}}", "startDate": "2026-12-01", "endDate": "2026-12-05", "price": 1 }

### Reset: put car 1 back to available after testing -> 200
PUT {{local}}/cars/{{car1}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeA}}

{ "status": "available" }

########## C11: car status (internal, Inspection only) ##########

### C11: car 4 -> maintenance -> 200
PATCH {{local}}/internal/cars/{{car4}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "maintenance" }

### C11: same again -> 200 (already in maintenance, nothing changes)
PATCH {{local}}/internal/cars/{{car4}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "maintenance" }

### C11: car 2 retired -> 409
PATCH {{local}}/internal/cars/{{car2}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "maintenance" }

### C11: car does not exist -> 404
PATCH {{local}}/internal/cars/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "maintenance" }

### C11: status "available" -> 400 (Inspection may only set maintenance)
PATCH {{local}}/internal/cars/{{car4}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "available" }

### C11: carId not a UUID -> 400
PATCH {{local}}/internal/cars/1/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "maintenance" }

### Reset: car 4 back to available (staff of office B) -> 200
PUT {{local}}/cars/{{car4}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-dev-user: staff:{{officeB}}

{ "status": "available" }

########## Cloud ##########

### Cloud health check -> 200 (once deploying works)
GET {{cloud}}/health
